Introduction

A conventional wisdom in the economics profession is that complete markets are good. The welfare theorems state that complete markets outcomes are Pareto optimal and that any optimal allocation can be realized by trade in complete markets with an appropriate lump-sum transfer scheme. So limits that close trading opportunities leave potential mutual gains unrealized.

